{"schema": 1, "kind": "review", "id": "rev-20261027T151904Z-1b759762", "ts": "2026-10-27T15:20:56Z", "actor": {"worktree": "prawduct", "plugin": "3.8.0-dev.1", "branch": "fix/stop-deferral-quiet"}, "body": {"base_commit": "7c4fb9ff8a461cd0fce5f483b08360e1274892c7", "base_tree": "6cb6809cb1b9f43abf026c1a44bbf3a66328a6c3", "head_tree": "7f10fe3f550c61fc47c6f64509db30befa2725b4", "head_commit": "f8dc5cc724026068a68c5f25397da9469ebb4024", "dispatch_commit": "f8dc5cc724026068a68c5f25397da9469ebb4024", "mode": "cumulative (bundle review, ready for merge)", "mode_chosen_by": "explicit-args", "stage": "boundary", "tier": "escalate", "roster": [{"role": "correctness", "model": "claude-opus-5-5"}, {"role": "design", "model": "claude-opus-5-5"}, {"role": "sustainability", "model": "claude-opus-5-5"}], "files_reviewed": ["plugin/bin/prawduct-hook", "tests/test_review_interval_extension.py", "tests/test_short_plan_deferral.py"], "files_changed": [".prawduct/artifacts/build-plan-stop-deferral-quiet.md", ".prawduct/changes/stop-deferral-quiet.md", "plugin/bin/prawduct-hook", "tests/test_review_interval_extension.py", "tests/test_short_plan_deferral.py"], "files_oracle": [".prawduct/artifacts/build-plan-stop-deferral-quiet.md", ".prawduct/changes/stop-deferral-quiet.md"], "findings": [{"goal": "Nothing Is Missing", "severity": "note", "title": "Requirements inventory still lists deferral notes as a systemMessage advisory", "recommendation": "documentation/issues/928-requirements.md row 7 says Stop advisories at exit 0 go out as `{systemMessage}`, and it names 'Deferral notes' among them. After this change the two deferral notices are stderr-log-only at exit 0. Add a clause to that row (e.g. 'except log-only advisories such as the deferred-boundary-review notice') so the host-porting inventory does not specify the old delivery. Core rule: 'A mechanism change is done when every artifact DESCRIBING it agrees'.", "files": ["plugin/bin/prawduct-hook"], "fid": "R-1"}, {"goal": "Nothing Is Broken", "severity": "note", "title": "Exit-2 delivery of the review-interval extension notice is not pinned by its own test", "recommendation": "The extension notice now reaches the model only when another gate blocks. That path goes through the same `_deliver_stop_advisories(blocking=True)` branch the short-plan exit-2 test exercises (test_short_plan_deferral.py ~537), so it is covered transitively. test_review_interval_extension.py has no test of its own showing the extension notice under 'ADVISORIES (not blocking):' at exit 2. Optional: add one so the claim 'still rides the exit-2 block text' is pinned for both notices.", "files": ["tests/test_review_interval_extension.py"], "fid": "R-2"}, {"goal": "Everything Is Coherent", "severity": "note", "title": "DEFERRED_REVIEW_TOKEN comment still says the token is for the transcript", "recommendation": "Instance. The comment above DEFERRED_REVIEW_TOKEN (plugin/bin/prawduct-hook ~L240) calls it 'one grep-able word for the transcript'. After this change, a turn that exits 0 never puts the token in the transcript. It appears in the stderr log, and in the exit-2 block text. Nothing reads this wording, and it misleads no one into doing anything. If it is touched, make it relational ('for whoever reads the notice'). No edit is wanted for its own sake.", "files": ["plugin/bin/prawduct-hook"], "fid": "R-3"}, {"goal": "Everything Is Coherent", "severity": "note", "title": "Test comment narrates the renegotiation history", "recommendation": "Instance. The comment in tests/test_short_plan_deferral.py (~L506) opens 'Renegotiated (2026-10-27, owner: \"pure noise\"): this used to be a `systemMessage`...'. That is review and decision history inside a shipped comment. review-protocol.md's prose-remedy rule treats such a comment as a deletion. The ruling already lives in the plan's 'Decisions made mid-build' and in the change fragment. Cut the comment to the invariant it pins ('log-only at exit 0; the exit-2 case carries it to the model; additionalContext unused because it starts a turn, #822').", "files": ["tests/test_short_plan_deferral.py"], "fid": "R-4"}, {"goal": "The Design Is Sound", "severity": "note", "title": "Audience encoded as a str subclass is lost by any string transform", "recommendation": "Instance; it is borderline and fine as built. `_LogOnlyAdvisory(str)` carries the advisory's audience as a type tag. Any later str operation on the list's items (strip, +, format, a rewrap pass before delivery) returns a plain str, and that silently brings the notice back to systemMessage. Nothing in cmd_stop does that today: both appends wrap the finished `_attributed(...)` text, and `_deliver_stop_advisories` filters by isinstance. If a third audience appears, or the documentation/issues/928 port lands (it already proposes `Advisory{text, audience}`), change this to an explicit (text, audience) record in one owner. No change is needed now.", "files": ["plugin/bin/prawduct-hook"], "fid": "R-5"}, {"goal": "Everything Is Coherent", "severity": "note", "title": "Unchanged docs still map deferral notes to the exit-0 systemMessage", "recommendation": "Class: prose describing where the Stop gate's deferral notice is delivered. Search 'systemMessage' and 'Stop gate WARNS'/'warns rather than blocks' outside archive/. documentation/issues/928-requirements.md row 7 (L261) lists 'Deferral notes' among the advisories rendered as `{systemMessage}` at exit 0. That is now false, and a Codex adapter designed from that row would resurface the notice this change removed. The row's own proposal (`Advisory{text, audience}`) should gain a log-only audience when the design stage picks it up. The L39 grounding fact is a dated measurement, so it is history and exempt. plugin/skills/critic/review-cycle.md L14 and plugin/methodology/planning.md L156 say the Stop gate 'warns'. That is still true, but the warning no longer reaches anyone on a turn that exits 0. Leave those two alone unless a reader is shown to rely on seeing it.", "files": ["documentation/issues/928-requirements.md"], "fid": "R-6"}, {"goal": "Decisions Were Deliberate", "severity": "note", "title": "#928 requirements still list deferral notes as a systemMessage at exit 0", "recommendation": "The change moves the deferral notices off `systemMessage`, and documentation/issues/928-requirements.md was not checked for that. Its response-shape inventory, row 7 (and the prose near line 39), still names 'Deferral notes' as an exit-0 `{systemMessage}` advisory. The #928 host-adapter design that follows from that draft would port the notice back into the user's transcript on Codex. hook-surface rule 'Moving a value into a NEW channel silently unwires readers of the old one \u2014 grep them before committing' applies: this doc is the one reader the tests did not cover. Scope: instance. Make row 7 relational, e.g. 'advisories not marked log-only', or add the `_LogOnlyAdvisory` audience to its `Advisory{text, audience}` column. Backlog: #928 is the only open item `affecting` the changed files, and it is not resolved by this work.", "files": ["plugin/bin/prawduct-hook"], "fid": "R-7"}, {"goal": "Decisions Were Deliberate", "severity": "note", "title": "Mid-build decisions for the owner", "recommendation": "Scope: none. The plan records one mid-build decision: the two tests that pinned #822's `systemMessage` delivery for the deferral notice were renegotiated in the open, and their content assertions moved to stderr. The owner's ruling settled it ('seems like pure noise?', then '1 now', 2026-10-27). The test comments and the change record document it. No alignment-pass miss: the response is recorded as Proceed, with the owner quoted. The Goals trace to that ruling, and the capability is reached through both deferral appends in cmd_stop.", "fid": "R-8"}, {"goal": "Decisions Were Deliberate", "severity": "note", "title": "Learnings Cross-Check: no regression found", "recommendation": "Scope: none. Read core.md, authoring.md, gates.md, hook-surface.md, release.md and tests.md, the list `learnings-files --for-diff` printed. Checked core 'A channel that is produced and never consumed is a DEFECT': the log-only notice keeps a consumer, the exit-2 block text the model reads, so it conforms. Checked tests 'When a deliberate change turns a passing test red, renegotiate the contract in the open': it was followed, with the reason documented inline and the stderr positive assertion kept before the absence assertion. No learnings rules were added or changed this cycle. The one rule-backed item is the #928 NOTE above.", "fid": "R-9"}, {"goal": "Decisions Were Deliberate", "severity": "note", "title": "Records Pass: oracle set clears no bar", "recommendation": "Scope: none. Covered both files in files_oracle: .prawduct/artifacts/build-plan-stop-deferral-quiet.md and .prawduct/changes/stop-deferral-quiet.md. Their claims match the code. Both deferral appends are wrapped in `_LogOnlyAdvisory`. At exit 0 such an advisory is mirrored to stderr only, and at exit 2 it still prints under ADVISORIES. The quoted 'Commit and carry on' text exists in critic_mode.py's extension wording. record_lint reported zero findings. Nothing ships false, misleads into action, or must stop the merge.", "fid": "R-10"}], "counts": {"blocking": 0, "warning": 0, "note": 10}, "observations": [], "duration_seconds": 420, "scope": "stop-deferral-quiet", "scope_chosen_by": "binding", "scope_unresolved_cause": null, "scope_reason": null, "base_extended_from": null, "chunks": ["01", "02"], "chunks_proposed": ["01", "02"], "chunk": "01", "base_reviewed": "7c4fb9ff8a461cd0fce5f483b08360e1274892c7", "record_lint": {"records": [".prawduct/artifacts/build-plan-stop-deferral-quiet.md", ".prawduct/changes/stop-deferral-quiet.md"], "chunk_graded": "01", "chunks_graded": ["01", "02"], "plan_graded": ".prawduct/artifacts/build-plan-stop-deferral-quiet.md", "findings": [], "unchecked": [], "counts": {"chunk-ref-missing": 0, "governed-by-gap": 0, "sui